@lang en
IMPORT `tasco-ch6-additional`

-- Tests for the decision and Chapter I. Every expected value is worked by hand from the figures
-- the rules print (the working is beside each group); none was copied from an evaluation. A
-- failing assertion is a finding about the source or the encoding, never a value to edit.

§ `Tests — the decision and Chapter I`

§§ `Decision 168/2024, Article 2`

-- Signed 17 October 2024, in force from 15 November 2024 (PDF page 1, handwritten; page 59 typed).
#ASSERT `the date the decision was signed` EQUALS YMD 2024 10 17
#ASSERT `the date the rules take effect` EQUALS YMD 2024 11 15
-- A contract concluded on 14 November 2024, the day before: declined, not answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `under these rules,` `a policy concluded before the rules took effect` `the answer is` TRUE BECAUSE "a contract concluded before 15 November 2024 is governed by Decision 53/2024, which is not in this encoding"
#ASSERT `under these rules,` `the standard policy` `the answer is` TRUE

§§ `Article 1.11 — months of use`

-- First registered March 2022, contract January 2025: (2025 x 12 + 1) - (2022 x 12 + 3) = 34.
#ASSERT `Article 1.11 — the months of use of the vehicle insured by` `the standard policy` EQUALS 34
-- Imported after use abroad, made 2015, counted from January 2015 to January 2025: 120.
#ASSERT `Article 1.11 — the months of use of the vehicle insured by` (`a policy on` `a used import made in 2015` `, own damage` 300000000 `, accident` 100000000 `, clauses` EMPTY) EQUALS 120

§§ `Article 1.12 — agreement by signing or paying`

#ASSERT `Article 1.12 — the policyholder has agreed to the information on` `the standard policy`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.12 — the policyholder has agreed to the information on` `a policy with the premium unpaid`

§§ `Article 1.17.2 — the deductible, both sides`

-- (a) at or below the deductible: nothing; (b) above it: the excess.
#ASSERT `Article 1.17.2 — the amount after a deductible of` 500000 `on` 500000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 1.17.2 — the amount after a deductible of` 500000 `on` 400000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 1.17.2 — the amount after a deductible of` 500000 `on` 500001 EQUALS 1

§§ `Article 2 — when the insurance is in force`

-- Period 10 January 2025 to 9 January 2026, both days in; premium paid.
#ASSERT `Article 2.1 — Tasco is liable under` `the standard policy` `for a loss on` (YMD 2025 1 10)
#ASSERT `Article 2.1 — Tasco is liable under` `the standard policy` `for a loss on` (YMD 2026 1 9)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2.1 — Tasco is liable under` `the standard policy` `for a loss on` (YMD 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2.1 — Tasco is liable under` `the standard policy` `for a loss on` (YMD 2025 1 9)
-- Premium unpaid: no liability, whatever the date.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2.1 — Tasco is liable under` `a policy with the premium unpaid` `for a loss on` (YMD 2025 6 15)
#ASSERT `Article 2.2 — the policy continues for the new owner` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2.2 — the policy continues for the new owner` TRUE TRUE

§§ `Article 3 — termination and refunds`

-- 3.1: paid 12 million, 5 million due to the end: refund 7 million; nothing after an insured event.
#ASSERT `Article 3.1 — the premium Tasco refunds, having received` 12000000 `against` 5000000 `, an insured event having happened:` FALSE EQUALS 7000000
#ASSERT `Article 3.1 — the premium Tasco refunds, having received` 12000000 `against` 5000000 `, an insured event having happened:` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 3.1 — the premium Tasco refunds, having received` 5000000 `against` 6000000 `, an insured event having happened:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Article 3.1 — the last day to settle the premium after the contract ended on` (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 16
#ASSERT NOT `Article 3.2.1 — a party may end the contract unilaterally` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Article 3.2.1 — a party may end the contract unilaterally` FALSE TRUE
-- Ended 11 July 2025: 182 of the period's 364 days left, a half.
#ASSERT `the fraction of the period of` `the standard policy` `left after` (YMD 2025 7 11) EQUALS 0.5
-- 3.2.2: 70% x 12,000,000 x 1/2 = 4,200,000; nothing after an insured event.
#ASSERT `Article 3.2.2 — the refund when the policyholder ends` `the standard policy` `by notice received on` (YMD 2025 7 11) `, an insured event having happened:` FALSE EQUALS 4200000
#ASSERT `Article 3.2.2 — the refund when the policyholder ends` `the standard policy` `by notice received on` (YMD 2025 7 11) `, an insured event having happened:` TRUE EQUALS 0
-- 3.2.3: 100% x 12,000,000 x 1/2 = 6,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 3.2.3 — the refund when Tasco ends` `the standard policy` `by notice issued on` (YMD 2025 7 11) EQUALS 6000000

§§ `Articles 4 and 5 — the deadlines`

GIVEN `received`     IS A MAYBE DATE
      `verification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `asked`        IS A MAYBE DATE
      `notice`       IS A MAYBE DATE
      `dispute`      IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A claim file`
`a file received` `received` `, verification:` `verification` `, authority asked` `asked` `, notice` `notice` `, dispute` `dispute` MEANS
    `A claim file` WITH
        `date the complete and valid file was received` IS `received`
        `verification needed`                           IS `verification`
        `date Tasco asked the authority to verify`      IS `asked`
        `date the settlement notice was received`       IS `notice`
        `date the dispute arose`                        IS `dispute`

GIVETH A `A claim file`
`a file received on 1 July 2025` MEANS `a file received` (JUST (YMD 2025 7 1)) `, verification:` FALSE `, authority asked` (JUST (YMD 2025 7 1)) `, notice` (JUST (YMD 2025 8 1)) `, dispute` (JUST (YMD 2025 9 1))

GIVETH A `A claim file`
`the same file, to be verified` MEANS `a file received` (JUST (YMD 2025 7 1)) `, verification:` TRUE `, authority asked` NOTHING `, notice` NOTHING `, dispute` NOTHING

GIVETH A `A claim file`
`no file yet` MEANS `a file received` NOTHING `, verification:` FALSE `, authority asked` NOTHING `, notice` NOTHING `, dispute` NOTHING

-- 4.2.4: 15 days, or 30 where the file must be verified.
#ASSERT `Article 4.2.4 — the last day for Tasco to pay, for` `a file received on 1 July 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `Article 4.2.4 — the last day for Tasco to pay, for` `the same file, to be verified` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 31
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 4.2.4 — the last day for Tasco to pay, for` `no file yet` BECAUSE "the payment period has not started, because no complete and valid claim file has been received"
-- 4.2.5: 90 days after the written request (1 July + 90 = 29 September).
#ASSERT `Article 4.2.5 — the day from which Tasco must verify the file itself` `a file received on 1 July 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 9 29
-- 4.2.6: a refusal explained within 15 days.
#ASSERT `Article 4.2.6 — the last day for Tasco to explain a refusal, for` `a file received on 1 July 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- 5.2.5: a change in risk notified within 05 days.
#ASSERT `Article 5.2.5 — the last day to notify Tasco of a change in risk made on` (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 6
-- 5.2.7(c): written notice within 5 days of a loss on 15 June: 20 June is in time, 21 June is not.
#ASSERT `Article 5.2.7(c) — the last day for written notice of a loss on` (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 20
#ASSERT `Article 5.2.7(c) — the duty to give written notice was met` `clean circumstances` (`conduct with notice` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 20)) `, moved:` FALSE `, recourse lost:` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5.2.7(c) — the duty to give written notice was met` `clean circumstances` (`conduct with notice` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 21)) `, moved:` FALSE `, recourse lost:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 5.2.7(c) — the duty to give written notice was met` `clean circumstances` `conduct with an objective obstacle and no notice`

-- The payment duty as a regulative rule: paid on day 15 is in time, day 16 is a breach.
#TRACE `Article 4.2.4 — Tasco must pay the claim` `a file received on 1 July 2025` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Tasco Insurance` DOES `pay the claim` AT 15
#TRACE `Article 4.2.4 — Tasco must pay the claim` `a file received on 1 July 2025` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)

§§ `Article 6 — the independent assessor's fee`

#ASSERT `Article 6.3 — who bears the independent assessor's fee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `as the court's judgment decides`
#ASSERT `Article 6.3 — who bears the independent assessor's fee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the policyholder bears it`
#ASSERT `Article 6.3 — who bears the independent assessor's fee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Tasco bears it`

§§ `Article 7 — the claim file`

GIVETH A `The kind of claim`
`a claim for a stolen car` MEANS
    `The kind of claim` WITH
        `damage to the vehicle or property`    IS FALSE
        `whole vehicle stolen or robbed`       IS TRUE
        `part of the vehicle stolen or robbed` IS FALSE
        `damage to goods carried`              IS FALSE
        `injury or death of a person`          IS FALSE
        `a person died`                        IS FALSE
        `claimed through an authorised person` IS FALSE
        `settled by conciliation`              IS FALSE
        `decided by a court`                   IS FALSE
        `a third party is liable`              IS FALSE
        `investigated by the police`           IS TRUE

#ASSERT elem `the decision to prosecute the theft or robbery` (`Article 7 — the documents the items name for` `a claim for a stolen car`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem `medical records of the injury` (`Article 7 — the documents the items name for` `a claim for a stolen car`))
#ASSERT elem `notice of loss and claim on Tasco's form` (`Article 7 — the documents the items name for` `a claim for a stolen car`)

§§ `Article 8 — double insurance`

#ASSERT `Article 8 — the contracts are double insurance` 1000000000 800000000
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8 — the contracts are double insurance` 800000000 800000000
-- Tasco insures 600 of 1,200 million: it pays half of 100 million.
#ASSERT `Article 8.1 — Tasco's share of` 100000000 `on a sum insured of` 600000000 `out of` 1200000000 EQUALS 50000000

§§ `Article 9 — time limits`

-- 9.1: one year from the loss of 15 June 2025; six days of force majeure push it to 21 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Article 9.1 — the last day to claim for the loss in` `clean circumstances` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15
#ASSERT `Article 9.1 — the last day to claim for the loss in` `circumstances with 6 days of force majeure` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 21
#ASSERT `Article 9.1 — a claim made on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `is in time for` `clean circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9.1 — a claim made on` (YMD 2026 6 16) `is in time for` `clean circumstances`
-- 9.2: 90 days from the settlement notice of 1 August 2025.
#ASSERT `Article 9.2 — the last day to complain about the settlement, for` `a file received on 1 July 2025` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 30
-- 9.3: 03 years from the dispute of 1 September 2025.
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the last day to sue on the contract, for` `a file received on 1 July 2025` EQUALS YMD 2028 9 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9.3 — the last day to sue on the contract, for` `no file yet` BECAUSE "no dispute has arisen, so the 03 years of Article 9.3 have not begun"

§§ `Article 10 — each exclusion, triggered and missed`

#ASSERT null (`Article 10 — the general exclusions that apply to` `clean circumstances` `of` `a private car`)
#ASSERT `Article 10.1 — the loss occurred outside Vietnam` `circumstances abroad in Laos`
#ASSERT `Article 10.2 — the loss was caused by war or terrorism` `circumstances of war`
#ASSERT `Article 10.3 — deliberate destruction by the policyholder, owner, driver or an interested person` `circumstances of deliberate destruction by the owner`
-- 10.4: an expired certificate excludes; one invalid only because of tyres within the maker's
-- specification does not; added seats save it only while the car is not over its persons.
#ASSERT `Article 10.4 — no valid inspection certificate` `circumstances with an expired inspection certificate` `a private car`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.4 — no valid inspection certificate` `circumstances with a certificate invalid only for changed tyres` `a private car`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.4 — no valid inspection certificate` `circumstances with added seats and 5 persons` `a private car`
#ASSERT `Article 10.4 — no valid inspection certificate` `circumstances with added seats and 6 persons` `a private car`
#ASSERT `Article 10.4 — no valid inspection certificate` `circumstances with a certificate invalid for another modification` `a private car`
-- 10.5: only while the vehicle is in operation; a suspended licence counts as none.
#ASSERT `Article 10.5 — the driver was under age or without a valid licence` `circumstances with an expired licence while driving`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.5 — the driver was under age or without a valid licence` `circumstances with an expired licence while parked`
#ASSERT `Article 10.5 — the driver was under age or without a valid licence` `circumstances with a suspended licence`
#ASSERT `Article 10.5 — the driver was under age or without a valid licence` `circumstances with an under-age driver`
#ASSERT `Article 10.6 — special equipment was operated without a required licence` `circumstances with unlicensed special equipment`
-- 10.7: over 50 mg/100 ml of blood or 0.25 mg/l of breath, "vượt quá" (strictly over).
#ASSERT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with blood alcohol of 51`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with blood alcohol of 50`
#ASSERT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with breath alcohol of 0.26`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with breath alcohol of 0.25`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with blood alcohol of 80 while parked`
#ASSERT `Article 10.7 — the driver was over the alcohol limit or had taken drugs` `circumstances with drugs`
-- 10.8: no causal link is asked for; a car parked where parking is prohibited is excluded even
-- though the parking did not cause the loss (finding X-07).
#ASSERT `Article 10.8 — a traffic offence at the time of the loss` `circumstances with a red light run`
#ASSERT `Article 10.8 — a traffic offence at the time of the loss` `circumstances with parking where prohibited`
#ASSERT `Article 10.9 — racing, unlawful towing, use in a crime, or prohibited goods` `circumstances with racing`
-- 10.10: a car of 5 persons: 8 on board is 60% over (excluded), 7 is 40% (not); a 10-tonne
-- truck: 15 t is exactly 50% (not, "trên 50%"), 15.1 t is 51% (excluded).
#ASSERT `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `circumstances with 8 persons` `a private car`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `circumstances with 7 persons` `a private car`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `circumstances with a load of 15 tonnes` `a truck`
#ASSERT `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `circumstances with a load of 15.1 tonnes` `a truck`
-- A special-purpose car: no basis is named. Not overloaded: nothing turns on it. Overloaded: declined.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `clean circumstances` `a crane truck`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10.10 — overloaded by more than half` `circumstances with a load of 12 tonnes` `a crane truck` BECAUSE "Article 10.10 names no basis for measuring the overload of a special-purpose car"
-- 10.11: 50% over the limit or more: 90 in a 60 zone is exactly 50% (excluded), 87 is 45% (not).
#ASSERT `Article 10.11 — speeding by half the limit or more` `circumstances at 90 in a 60 zone`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10.11 — speeding by half the limit or more` `circumstances at 87 in a 60 zone`
-- The list form, as the chapters read it.
#ASSERT `Article 10 — the general exclusions that apply to` `circumstances abroad in Laos` `of` `a private car` EQUALS LIST `10.1 outside Vietnam`
#ASSERT `Article 10 — the general exclusions that apply to` `circumstances at 90 in a 60 zone` `of` `a private car` EQUALS LIST `10.11 speeding by half or more`
